Story: TODOLIST-S2
Title: Add Comments to Open Tasks

User story:
As a task owner, I want to add comments to an open task so that I can record context and notes while working continuously whenever I interact with my open or past tasks, while closed task owners and non-owners are refused.

Acceptance criteria:
- Given an open task exists in the system, when the task owner submits a text comment payload, then the system appends the comment to that specific open task with a timestamp.
- Given a task is marked as closed, when a user attempts to add a comment to it, then the system refuses the addition and returns a 403 Forbidden status code.
- Given the task owner submits a comment, when it is stored and logged, then application logs omit any restricted data ensuring that application logs must not contain email addresses, phone numbers, government identifiers, or payment card data.

Technical notes:
- Accept text comment payload on POST /tasks/{id}/comments when the task is open and the actor is the task owner. Details: validate task status is open on the backend service when the endpoint runs; append comment with timestamp to the task storage; return 403 Forbidden when the task is marked as closed or the user is a non-owner; do not invent new notification services.
- Omit restricted data from application logs during comment submission and processing. Details: verify logger calls exclude email addresses, phone numbers, government identifiers, or payment card data as mandated by the logging policy when error handling or request tracing runs; do not log raw request bodies.

Out of scope:
Any automated task scheduling, third-party calendar synchronizations, external notification dispatches, and multi-user assignment workflows are out of scope.

Coder hint:
Validate task status and ownership before appending comments, ensuring closed tasks reject requests with a 403 status and logs remain strictly free of PII.

Implement that slice. Stay on this branch. Do not merge to the default branch.